  "caveats": [
    "wdl_acc and optimal_move_rate come from training/eval.py, which scores a GREEDY 1-ply engine over uniformly sampled positions. They saturate near 0.968; the 0.9969 headline figure in vs_god_results.json comes from the 3-ply minimax engine in evaluation/vs_god.py.",
    "The `incidents` column is not a diversity-bearing metric: every game in training/eval.py starts from the same root (0,0,[5]*10) with a deterministic engine and a deterministic oracle reply, so all games of a given parity are byte-identical and `incidents` scales linearly with --games (it equals n_games in 27 of 36 records). This degeneracy is exactly why evaluation/vs_god.py samples random symmetric starts instead; treat vs_god_results.json as the benchmark of record.",
    "n_positions and n_games vary across checkpoints (1 to 500,000 positions), so accuracy values from different rows carry different confidence. The 10,000-position rows from step 53976 onward are directly comparable to one another."
  ],
  "note_on_steps": "Steps 1..158976 were logged by training/eval.py during the continuous-learning run. The final match in vs_god_results.json was played by the step-394852 checkpoint, which post-dates this history."
}